# Offline preview output (Tools/AuroraPreview). Renders are large, binary, and regenerable from the
# shipped pure core in about a second, so they are working artifacts rather than source — a 7 MB GIF
# in history is permanent, and the field it shows is not. Keep them here while iterating; attach the
# two or three that matter to the PR instead of committing them.
Tools/AuroraPreview/renders/

# Offline preview output (Tools/VectorLightPreview), same reasoning as AuroraPreview's above: these
# regenerate from the shipped pure core in well under a second, so they are working artifacts rather
# than source. The three that were worth keeping are committed under Tests/Screenshots/ instead.
Tools/VectorLightPreview/out/

# Unity's own working directories for Tools/ShaderBundle. Library/ alone is hundreds of megabytes of
# regenerable import cache, and it is rebuilt from Assets/ + ProjectSettings/ on the first headless
# run. The three BUILT bundles under 1.6/AssetBundles/ ARE committed and deliberately not ignored:
# they are what ships, and requiring a 20 GB Unity install to compile this mod is not a trade anyone
# would take. See Tools/ShaderBundle/build.sh.
Tools/ShaderBundle/Library/
Tools/ShaderBundle/Logs/
Tools/ShaderBundle/Temp/
Tools/ShaderBundle/UserSettings/
Tools/ShaderBundle/obj/
